Aerie-Purpose: Register the Widevine component with the component updater only after the user opts in, and register the opt-in prefs in Local State.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/component_updater/registration.cc (RegisterComponentsForUpdate), chrome/browser/prefs/browser_prefs.cc (RegisterLocalState), the two BUILD.gn files and components/BUILD.gn (unit tests)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Widevine is built (enable_widevine=true) but is not downloaded, registered or enabled
until the user turns it on. RegisterWidevineCdmComponent(cus) used to run at every
startup; it now runs through aerie_widevine::RegisterWhenEnabled(), which calls it once,
at startup if aerie.widevine.enabled is true, or when the pref later turns true. With the
pref off the component updater never learns about Widevine, so nothing fetches it. The
CDM hint file that an earlier opt-in left in the profile is still read at startup; see
docs/widevine.md.

The component update URL for an opted-in browser is the next patch.

--- a/chrome/browser/component_updater/registration.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/component_updater/registration.cc
@@ -88,4 +88,5 @@
 #if BUILDFLAG(ENABLE_WIDEVINE_CDM_COMPONENT)
 #include "chrome/browser/component_updater/widevine_cdm_component_installer.h"
+#include "components/aerie_widevine/widevine_opt_in.h"
 #endif  // BUILDFLAG(ENABLE_WIDEVINE_CDM_COMPONENT)
 
@@ -148,5 +149,9 @@
 
 #if BUILDFLAG(ENABLE_WIDEVINE_CDM_COMPONENT)
-  RegisterWidevineCdmComponent(cus);
+  // Aerie: Widevine is opt-in. It is registered, and so downloaded, only once
+  // the user turns it on (Settings, or the prompt on the first DRM request).
+  aerie_widevine::RegisterWhenEnabled(
+      g_browser_process->local_state(),
+      base::BindRepeating(&RegisterWidevineCdmComponent, cus));
 #endif  // BUILDFLAG(ENABLE_WIDEVINE_CDM_COMPONENT)
 
